{0 Inspector}

Under [silica dev], a program can read what the machines of the app do while
it runs: the instance tree, the state and data of each machine, each step as
it happens, and the timers and sources that run. Each open page of the app is
one target, and the server is one more target for its Live islands. The
messages of all targets come in one stream, and each message names its
target.

The inspector exists only under [silica dev]. It uses what [silica dev]
already serves: the Unix socket [_build/silica-dev/inspect.sock] (mode 600,
for this user only) and a WebSocket at [/_silica/inspect] on the dev port of
[127.0.0.1], which refuses another [Origin]. A server with no [dev] config
does not connect to it, and a release bundle holds no inspector code; tests
check both.

{1:command silica inspect}

Run these from the root of the app while [silica dev] runs. Text is the
default; [--json] prints the protocol messages, one per line.

- [silica inspect targets]: the pages and the server.
- [silica inspect tree [--target T] [--machine ID] [--path PATH]]: each
  running instance with its machine, state, the timers and sources that run,
  and its snapshot and props when the machine registered its codecs (see
  {!Silica.Machine.register_codecs}). The props are the last ones the parent
  gave, also when the machine ignored them.
- [silica inspect tail [--target T] [--machine ID]... [--path PATH]
  [--event NAME]... [--change CHANGE]... [--count N]]: each step from now on.
  [--path] keeps the instance and the instances under it.
- [silica inspect export [--target T] [-o FILE]]: the last 5000 steps of a
  page as a trace file (see {!Silica.Trace}), for [silica inspect replay],
  [silica replay] and [silica conform]. With no [--target], the one page.
- [silica inspect replay FILE [--machine ID]]: runs [silica replay] on the
  root machine of the trace, or on [ID]. The root machine selects the entry
  whose root it is, such as [panel+preview] for [panel].
- [silica inspect graph ID [--specs DIR]]: each golden spec of the machine
  in [DIR] ([ID.spec.json] or [ID.spec.txt], and [<entry id>.ID.spec.json] or
  [<entry id>.ID.spec.txt] of each joint check), as a [spec FILE] line and the
  text form, then a [current] line for each running instance, a [seen] line
  for each edge that the app took and one of the specs has, and a [drift]
  line for each edge the app took that no spec has. The edges are the ones of
  every page since [silica dev] started, also before a reload. With no spec,
  the graph that the app took, under the line [not checked].

Exit code 0: done; 1: the hub answered with an error; 3: no [silica dev] runs
here, or bad arguments.

A press on the button "Vote" of the example, then on "Increment" of its Live
counter, as [silica inspect tail] prints them:

{v
[tab-002d] 8 router/:home/4:vote idle -> loading (entered) on load <- press button "Vote" (div > div > button) => start call 5.1/vote/loading//api/vote null /api/vote
[tab-002d] 10 router/:home/4:vote loading -> ready (entered) on settled ok <- answer /api/vote ["Ok",1] => stop 5.1/vote/loading//api/vote null
[server] 2 counter#ef03bf4a1a927e8c counter -> counter (kept) on incr <- message
v}

The instance path of a Live island is its machine id, [#], and the instance
id of the island in the page.

{1:protocol The protocol}

Each message is one JSON object with a field ["t"]. On the Unix socket each
message is one line; on the WebSocket, one text frame. The first message of a
connection is a [hello] with ["version":1] and a role: [target] or [client].
A [hello] with another version gets an [error] and the connection closes. A
client request can carry an ["id"]; the answers carry it. The OCaml types and
codecs are in {!Silica.Inspect}.

The examples below are real lines of the example app under [silica dev].

{2:targets What a target sends}

A target sends these, and the hub forwards them to the clients that
subscribed. The hub keeps the tree of each target and its last 5000 steps.

[hello] starts a target. The hub forwards it to the clients when the target
connects:

{v
{"t":"hello","role":"target","version":1,"target":"tab-002d","kind":"browser","url":"/"}
{"t":"hello","role":"target","version":1,"target":"server","kind":"server"}
v}

[tree] gives every running instance, parents first. A target sends it when it
connects again; the hub answers a [tree] request with it:

{v
{"t":"tree","id":3,"target":"server","instances":[{"path":"counter#ef03bf4a1a927e8c","machine":"counter","state":"counter","data":1,"owns":[]}]}
v}

[mount] is an instance that started, with its state, data, props and
[owns], the timers, calls, subscriptions and held sources that run during its
snapshot, with the time each started:

{v
{"t":"mount","target":"tab-002d","path":"router/:home/3:votes","machine":"votes","state":"watching","owns":[{"kind":"subscription","id":"4.0/votes/watching/live:votes main","topic":"votes","since":1794454000361.0}]}
v}

[step] is one record of the transition log as {!Silica.Transition.codec}
writes it, with [target] and [owns] (what runs during the snapshot after the
step; left out for an [unhandled] step). [data] and [snapshot] are there when the
machine registered its codecs:

{v
{"t":"step","target":"tab-002d","seq":8,"time_ms":1794454000940.0,"instance":"router/:home/4:vote","number":5,"entry":1,"machine":"vote","from":"idle","to":"loading","change":"entered","event":"load","actions":["start call 5.1/vote/loading//api/vote null /api/vote"],"cause":{"type":"element","handler":"press","role":"button","name":"Vote","element":"div > div > button"},"owns":[{"kind":"call","id":"5.1/vote/loading//api/vote null","path":"/api/vote","since":1794454000940.0}]}
{"t":"step","target":"server","seq":2,"time_ms":1794454001454.202,"instance":"counter#ef03bf4a1a927e8c","number":1,"entry":0,"machine":"counter","from":"counter","to":"counter","change":"kept","event":"incr","data":["Incr"],"snapshot":1,"cause":{"type":"message"},"owns":[]}
v}

[unmount] is an instance that ended, after its [ended] step:

{v
{"t":"unmount","target":"tab-002d","path":"router/:home/3:votes"}
v}

[resumed] is a hot reload: the instances that kept their state, and the ones
that started again with the reason:

{v
{"t":"resumed","target":"tab-002d","kept":["router","router/:about"],"restarted":[]}
v}

Two messages have their format now and are not sent yet. [live] will carry
the messages of a Live socket, and [paused] will say that a target is paused
at a step (time travel):

{v
{"t":"live","target":"server","dir":"in","channel":"counter","message":"{\"t\":\"event\",\"event\":[\"Increment\"]}"}
{"t":"paused","target":"tab-3f2a","at":42}
v}

{2:clients What a client sends}

[hello] starts a client. The hub answers with [targets]:

{v
{"t":"hello","role":"client","version":1,"name":"silica-inspect"}
{"t":"targets","targets":[{"target":"server","kind":"server"}]}
v}

[subscribe] forwards the messages of one [target], or of every target, from
now on. The [filter] keeps the steps of the listed machines ([machine]), of an
instance and the instances under it ([path]), of the listed events ([event])
and changes ([change]); mounts and unmounts pass by machine and path. The hub
answers [subscribed]:

{v
{"t":"subscribe","id":1,"filter":{}}
{"t":"subscribed","id":1}
v}

A filter with each field, as [silica inspect tail --target tab-002d --machine
vote --path router --event load --change entered] sends it:

{v
{"t":"subscribe","id":1,"target":"tab-002d","filter":{"machine":["vote"],"path":"router","event":["load"],"change":["entered"]}}
v}

[targets] lists the targets:

{v
{"t":"targets","id":2}
{"t":"targets","id":2,"targets":[{"target":"server","kind":"server"},{"target":"tab-002d","kind":"browser","url":"/"}]}
v}

[tree] with no [instances] asks for the tree of one target, or of each target
with no [target]: one [tree] answer for each.

{v
{"t":"tree","id":3}
v}

[export] asks for the steps that the hub kept for a target, as a trace file in
the field [trace] of the answer:

{v
{"t":"export","id":5,"target":"server"}
{"t":"trace","id":5,"target":"server","trace":"{\"root\":\"counter\",\"build\":\"dev\",\"origin\":{\"type\":\"runtime\",\"platform\":\"server\"},\"dropped\":0}\n{\"seq\":1,\"time_ms\":1794453604567.145,\"instance\":\"counter#dbe0cc4ee340b863\",\"number\":1,\"entry\":0,\"machine\":\"counter\",\"from\":\"\",\"to\":\"counter\",\"change\":\"started\",\"event\":\"\",\"snapshot\":0,\"cause\":{\"type\":\"start\"}}\n{\"seq\":2,\"time_ms\":1794453605969.875,\"instance\":\"counter#dbe0cc4ee340b863\",\"number\":1,\"entry\":0,\"machine\":\"counter\",\"from\":\"counter\",\"to\":\"counter\",\"change\":\"kept\",\"event\":\"incr\",\"data\":[\"Incr\"],\"snapshot\":1,\"cause\":{\"type\":\"message\"}}\n"}
v}

[seen] asks for the steps of a machine that the hub got from every target
since [silica dev] started, also from pages that reloaded: one step of each
kind (change, states, event), with no user data. [silica inspect graph]
reads its edges from it:

{v
{"t":"seen","id":6,"machine":"counter"}
{"t":"seen","id":6,"machine":"counter","steps":[{"seq":1,"time_ms":1794453604567.145,"instance":"counter#dbe0cc4ee340b863","number":1,"entry":0,"machine":"counter","from":"","to":"counter","change":"started","event":"","cause":{"type":"start"}}]}
v}

[travel] and [live] with no [dir] will pause a target at a step and leave
time travel. They get an [error] now:

{v
{"t":"travel","id":4,"target":"server","seq":1}
{"t":"error","id":4,"message":"time travel is not available yet"}
v}

[gone] says that a target disconnected, such as a page that closed or a
server that restarts:

{v
{"t":"gone","target":"server"}
v}
